✅ Final Library Management UML (SDE-2)
1. Book (metadata only)
Book
----------------
- isbn : String
- title : String
- author : String
+ getters


Book never moves. It is only metadata.

2. BookCopy (physical copy)
BookCopy
----------------
- copyId : String
- book : Book
- isAvailable : boolean
+ issue()
+ return()
+ isAvailable()


This is what gets issued.

3. User
User
----------------
- id : String
- name : String
+ getters


User does not track issued books.

4. Loan/IssuedBook (most important entity)
Loan
----------------
- copy : BookCopy
- user : User
- issueDate : LocalDate
+ getters


Tracks lifecycle of issue/return.

5. Catalog (search component)
Catalog
----------------
- Map<String, List<BookCopy>>  // isbn → copies
+ addBookCopy(BookCopy)
+ searchByIsbn(String isbn) : List<BookCopy>


Separates search from business logic.

6. FineStrategy (Strategy pattern)
FineStrategy
----------------
+ calculateFine(LocalDate issueDate) : double

Implementation
DefaultFineStrategy
WeekendFineStrategy (optional)

7. LibraryService (brain / orchestrator)
LibraryService
----------------
- catalog : Catalog
- activeLoans : Map<String, Loan>   // copyId → loan
- fineStrategy : FineStrategy

+ issueBook(isbn, user) : Loan
+ returnBook(copyId) : double


All decisions happen here.

Relationships (say this while drawing)

BookCopy references Book

Loan references BookCopy and User

Catalog stores BookCopy

LibraryService uses Catalog and FineStrategy

LibraryService creates and removes Loan

10-second explanation you should give

Book is metadata, BookCopy is the physical entity that gets issued, Loan tracks the lifecycle, Catalog handles search, and LibraryService orchestrates issue/return using a pluggable FineStrategy.

Memory Hook
Book → BookCopy → Loan → LibraryService


This is the correct mental chain.
